==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*skiljaną||to separate, limit}}, from {{inh|non|ine-pro|*(s)kelH-||to split, cut}}. Compare {{etyl|xcl|-}} {{m|xcl|ցելում|}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|scylian}}, {{m|ang|scielian||to divide, separate}}. More at {{l|en|skill}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb}}

# to [[part]], [[divide]], [[separate]]
# to [[break off]], [[break up]]
# to part company, take leave
# to [[distinguish]], [[discern]]
# to [[understand]], [[find out]]
# to [[decide]], [[settle]]
# to set apart, reserve for one

===References===
* {{R:non:Zoega}}

